ARRAYLIST -- resizable/dynamic array
    -- collection framework of java
    -- java.util.Arraylist
    -- use when Frequent access
    -- do not use when Heavy insert/delete in middle
    -- ArrayList is NOT synchronized.

*IQ* can arraylist store primitive data type? -- NO
        -- it uses Wrapper class
        -- Java Collections (like ArrayList, HashMap, etc.) store objects only, not primitives.

*IQ* Is arrayllist slower than array? -- YES
        -- Dynamic resizing, Extra memory overhead,Stores objects (not primitives directly)

